  "_comment": "SYNC_PROTOCOL.md §10.6: what a message.deleted does to the conversation's unread and mention counts on every client (2026-10-09, a DM or a mention deleted before it was read kept its red badge). Applied before the tombstone replaces the held row. channel: the counts as held, counted_to = the channel's last_seq before the event (the counts cover every change up to it: the bootstrap's, read.updated's and the live events'). event_seq: the deletion's seq (the tombstone's updated_seq). message: the tombstone (the server clears its mentions, so whether it mentioned me is known only from the held row). held: the row this device holds for it before the event (null = not held), mentions_me with the live rule (mention_all, mentioned_user_ids, my notify_keywords). The deletion is subtracted when it was counted: event_seq > counted_to, someone else's, type user, in the timeline (no parent, or also_in_channel), seq > last_read_seq, not already deleted here, unread > 0. Then unread - 1; mentions - 1 when the held row mentions me (never below 0); not held: mentions stay and refetch when mentions > 0. unread 0: mentions 0, first_unread_at null, no refetch. The deleted row was the first unread (its created_at == first_unread_at) and some remain: first_unread_at stays and refetch. refetch: ask the server (PUT /channels/{id}/read {last_read_seq: 0}, a no-op answering the read state) and take its counts like read.updated. Hand-written; Desktop / Web, iOS and Android test against it.",
